LOOMA — MASTER ARCHITECTURE TRANSFORMATION & IMPLEMENTATION

Two Independent Platform Experiences Within One Application

Project: Looma
Repository: https://github.com/PRIGID-WEB-CLOUD/Looma-
Primary objective: Transform Looma into one unified application containing two genuinely independent platform experiences:

1. NORMAL PLATFORM — Personal social networking.
2. BUSINESS PLATFORM — Professional social networking, business communication and commerce.

Development approach: Repository-aware, audit-first, phased implementation, backend-enforced security, reversible migrations and comprehensive testing.

---

0. EXECUTIVE PROJECT DIRECTIVE

You are working on Looma, an existing social networking and commerce platform.

Your responsibility is to inspect, architect, correct and implement a complete two-platform architecture within the existing application.

These are NOT two profile types that merely display different names, avatars or badges.

They must function as two distinct application environments with different:

- Interfaces and layouts.
- Navigation systems.
- Features and workflows.
- Identity contexts.
- Data ownership.
- Messaging environments.
- Notifications and activity.
- Settings.
- Permissions.
- Commerce capabilities.

Both platforms belong to one mother account and share carefully selected underlying infrastructure.

The user must be able to switch between the two environments seamlessly, similar to Facebook's multiple-profile switching experience, but with significantly more independent functionality.

Critical distinction: Profile switching is not the same as platform switching.

Changing the active profile must activate the entire corresponding platform experience.

Do not create two unrelated applications. Do not duplicate the entire backend. Build two independent application experiences using shared infrastructure where appropriate.

