FINAL ULTIMATE OBJECTIVE

Build Looma as one unified application containing two independent platform experiences:

NORMAL: A complete personal social networking platform.

BUSINESS: A complete professional social networking, customer communication and commerce platform.

They share the underlying Looma infrastructure, but maintain their own identities, interfaces, data ownership, permissions, messaging environments, settings and functional capabilities.

The mother account provides the authentication foundation.

The personal profile remains the human identity.

Business Profiles remain independent organizational identities.

Memberships define business authority.

Platform switching activates the entire corresponding application environment.

Never confuse profile switching with platform switching.

Never confuse a human account with a business organization.

Never sacrifice existing user data or working commerce functionality to achieve the new architecture.

The objective is not simply to redesign Looma. It is to transform its underlying architecture and deliver two genuinely independent experiences within one coherent application.